						21:30 Sunday, 27 April 1986

Dear Tina,

     Once upon a time, when I still had the impression that you cared, perhaps
not for, but at least about me, this letter would have been a detailed summary
of my trip.  Now, of course, I'm not even sure I will even send it to you.  I
really miss the fun of seeing new places with the eye of a reporter/philosopher
eagerly looking for things to tell you about.  'You could pick someone else to
write to', I can almost hear you saying, 'it doesn't have to be me.'  And of
course that's true, though I don't know anyone else in a comparable situation,
i.e. distant, so that writing is the only practical method of communication,
and also so that writing is also important as a way to learn about each other.
